"The keepers hold that a waking dragon ends the age of men, so every dragon must be stilled."
"The Well was the only source of the blood the chain-makers quench their iron in."
"Iron quenched once the Stillwater's cistern runs dry takes no bite."
"The chain-makers keep seven houses; the Stillwater was one, and the three towers are another."
"The chain-makers' house in the northern peaks has been empty since Eira broke free there."
"The Stillwater sent its tally downriver to the market every seventh dusk."
"The first tally the Stillwater misses falls on the third dusk after the dawn Alan woke in the Well."
"Three days after a missed tally, a Hand of the order comes upriver with rangers and wyrm-riders."
"With the Well dark, the chain-makers mean to make Eira their new Well."
"The chain-makers cannot open Eira's ice, and keep a camp at its edge, waiting for whoever can."
